<!--
  Combat Extended and the pads' Dismember (CE 16.7.4). The fields are DismemberExtension's,
  their rules in the headers of Ability_Dismember.Strike.cs and MeleeAim.cs.

  damage 80, where the main tree has 60. CE leaves the strike itself alone (the header of
  Ability_Dismember.Strike.cs has why) and keeps vanilla's scale of damage against part health,
  but it raises a leg's hitPoints from 30 to 40, a human's and a mechanoid's, softens Tough from
  half damage to 0.66 and adds five hit points to each ring of a centipede. 80 is the main
  tree's 60 by that 40 over 30, which keeps what the def header says of 60: a Tough human loses
  a leg (52.8 against 40) as surely as an arm, a muffalo's leg (70) comes off, and a centipede's
  last ring (108) only for a pilot in the hemogen rush (120). It sits where CE puts a
  warcasket's own melee, between its broadsword's edge (68) and its gravity hammer's head (92).
  CE reads no armor penetration off a strike that ignores armor, so there is none to give.

  aimHeightComp and aimHeightField: CE gives every humanlike a CompMeleeTargettingGizmo and a
  colonist with Melee 8 a button that cycles its heightInt through automatic, low, middle and
  high, which CE's melee verb follows for a player pawn. Named here, the strike follows it too:
  low takes a leg, middle an arm, and high, where a human has no limb, either
  (DismemberTarget). The field is CE's own save data, so nothing of ours is stored.

  Tests/1.6/CompatPatchTests.cs holds the fields named here to the ones the C# declares.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef[defName="HPWC_Dismember"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="HemophageWarcasket.DismemberExtension"]/damage</xpath>
    <value>
      <damage>80</damage>
    </value>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef[defName="HPWC_Dismember"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="HemophageWarcasket.DismemberExtension"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <aimHeightComp>CombatExtended.CompMeleeTargettingGizmo</aimHeightComp>
      <aimHeightField>heightInt</aimHeightField>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
